doc('03-auth-account-route-state-permission-matrix.md','Routes, aliases, states and authority',f'{ev("route-state-matrix.json")} has {len(matrix)} distinct surfaces and {len(matrix)*len(states)} explicit state cells. TESTED refers to its named unit/fixture/browser layer; SOURCE-MAPPED is not a completed journey. No all-route-state percentage is claimed. Source inventory remains 135 routes / 62 groups / 63 app-group pairs.\n\n'+table(['Surface','Guard / role','Authority','Evidence'],[(r['surface'],r['guard'],r['authority'],r['source'])for r in matrix])+f'\n\n{source("apps/frontend-user/src/layouts/AuthShell.jsx")} permits authenticated visits. {source("apps/frontend-user/src/app/routes/hostRoutes.jsx","function AccountRedirect")} guards account aliases and preserves search/hash. There is no email-verification route or new provider invented by this phase.')
doc('04-auth-contract-backend-policy-and-security-review.md','Server contracts and security review',table(['Endpoint','Actual policy','Source'],[(r['endpoint'],r['policy'],source(r['source']))for r in contracts])+f'\n\nBackend auth/account/architecture check: **{result("backend-auth-wrapper")}**. Maven PATH lookup failed; the repository wrapper succeeded with JDK25. Maven emitted optional repository metadata401 warnings; no auth service/test failure. No MySQL/staging/provider certification.\n\n{source(auth+"safeRedirect.js")} retains same-origin path allowlists. {source("apps/frontend-admin/src/app/guards/RequireAdmin.jsx")} requires actual ADMIN and uses separate storage. Server token, role, ownership, entitlements and prices remain authoritative. No verified P0 credential disclosure, external open redirect or role bypass was reproduced. C08-003 is bounded privacy repair, not proof of transport secrecy.')
doc('05-login-register-and-password-visibility.md','Login, registration and password controls',f'{source(auth+"LoginFeature.jsx","handleSubmit")} trims identifiers and preserves entered identifier on 400/401/403/429/500/offline failure. Pending Enter/click is suppressed. Browser C08 pending test verifies pointer caret selection and keyboard Space without form submit. Toggles remain type=button with localized names and aria-pressed. Autofill remains username/current-password/new-password.\n\n{source(auth+"RegisterFeature.jsx","passwordRequirements")} keeps fullName/phone/password DTO and five rules. Existing tests cover7/8/100/101 units, Khmer letters/digits, all-uppercase and confirmation; C08-002 adds the DTO Lu edge. Java chars and JavaScript split intentionally do not treat a supplementary character as a single BMP letter. No lowercase rejection is added.\n\nFull native touch/AT behavior and every field/error association are not certified. Refer to `RegisterFeature.test.jsx`, `LoginFeature.test.jsx`, `Phase08Regression.test.jsx` and `phase08-codex-regression.spec.js`.')
doc('06-forgot-reset-password-and-private-recovery.md','Private recovery and reset',f'{source(auth+"ForgotPasswordFeature.jsx","Request received")} confirms request receipt conditionally and ignores arbitrary response/error text that could reveal existence. 429/500/offline are errors with retained email and retry. Receipt is not SMTP delivery. Phone-only registration has no proven self-service email attachment/recovery path; `/contact` is assistance, not identity verification. Khmer changes reuse existing conditional/check-inbox/contact wording; native approval remains open and no linguistic certification is claimed.\n\n{source(auth+"ResetPasswordFeature.jsx","clean.delete")} consumes link tokens into component state and replaces history search. Link tokens do not render in a field; manual entry remains masked. Success clears token/password/confirmation and invalidates local sessions; failure exposes manual another-token fallback. Invalid/expired/reused responses are synthetic, not real server token consumption. {source("apps/frontend-user/index.html","referrer")} sets no-referrer before resource links. The initial document URL can still reach hosting logs, browser history before replacement or an extension; deployment policy must be checked separately. No token is returned by the recovery API in dev or production.')
doc('07-oauth-google-telegram-and-provider-failures.md','Google and Telegram boundaries',f'{source(auth+"components/SocialAuthButtons.jsx","function loadScript")} retries failed script nodes on remount; C08-009 fails before and passes after. Unit fixtures also verify server account-link conflicts and authenticated linking. Real Google-rendered button is retained. Telegram popup accepts messages only from oauth.telegram.org and the opened window; blocked/closed popup handling and SDK/widget modes remain in source. {source(auth+"components/telegramOAuth.js")} owns URL generation.\n\nProvider configured/unconfigured branches, cancellation, state/nonce expiry and live account linking are not exhaustively browser-certified. Local production-like builds block external resources; no real tokens, accounts or provider callbacks were used. English-only provider diagnostics in Khmer and setup terminology remain a native/copy-owner review item. Live provider sandboxes are BLOCKED — EXTERNAL. No fabricated provider success or new login method.')
doc('08-profile-avatar-change-password-and-logout.md','Profile, media and password lifecycle',f'{source(auth+"ProfileFeature.jsx","setLoadFailed")} now distinguishes GET failure from editable profile data and offers retry. Fetch effects ignore late completion and re-run for account ID/retry, not every store object. Save suppresses duplicates, uses server canonical data, does not fabricate profileComplete and retains a successful uploaded URL for PATCH retry. Readers abort on replacement/unmount; broken-image UI does not clear the stored URL. MIME/extension/nonempty/5MiB client checks complement server signature and configured size checks. Native image decoder/content/ownership/storage integration remains server/staging work.\n\nTests cover invalid/oversize avatar, failed upload, PATCH retry, canonical store update and profile load recovery. Explicit cancellation and every stale account-switch race are source-mapped, not exhaustively executed. No automatic deletion of uploaded storage objects is invented.\n\n{source(auth+"ChangePasswordFeature.jsx","void logout")} and the embedded form use the same four account rules and immediate post-success logout. {source("apps/frontend-user/src/stores/useAuthStore.js","broadcast = false")} supports reset invalidation broadcast without revoking an unrelated server account. Backend tokenVersion invalidation remains unchanged.')
doc('09-session-bootstrap-guards-redirects-and-roles.md','Sessions, guards and safe return',f'{source("apps/frontend-user/src/stores/useAuthStore.js","initializeSession")} retains generation protection, one in-flight cookie bootstrap, anonymous401/403 versus retryable5xx/offline error, validated response shape and bearer expiry. `useAuthStore.test.js` and `AuthProvider.test.jsx` exercise restoration, late bootstrap after logout, cross-tab logout and expired bearer. Cookie-mode browser build is not separately certified.\n\n{source("apps/frontend-user/src/app/guards/RequireAuth.jsx","authStatus")} shows checking skeleton before content, localized error retry and complete path/query/hash return. C08-007 rejects malformed or nested credential-bearing next targets without removing valid template intent. Dashboard aliases and `/profile` remain under the auth guard. Historical admin boundary tests cover USER/STAFF/unsupported roles, expired token and customer storage isolation; UI guards never grant backend admin authority.')
doc('10-premium-visual-theme-typography-and-component-qa.md','Silk & Ink visual and component QA',f'Warm canvas, forest ink, restrained gold, brand/home return, preference controls and conventional form hierarchy were retained. {ev("visual-capture-manifest.json")} pairs24 initial locale/theme scenes and adds24 current API-error scenes; all media is fictional. Profile and password pages retain owner chrome. No renderer artwork, font asset, canonical token sheet or admin stylesheet changed.\n\n{source(auth+"ChangePasswordFeature.css")} now scopes extracted styles, avoiding HostShell dash-main collisions. {source(auth+"ProfileFeature.css")} reserves eye-button space and long-name wrapping. C08-012 fixes real dark hint/link/provider error and owner account-pill contrast. See {ev("contrast-before-repair.json")} versus {ev("contrast-results.json")}; all ordinary scans are separate from forced-colors computed-color results. Loaded local font and diacritic appearance are evidence for inspection, not native Khmer approval.')
doc('11-responsive-accessibility-language-and-input.md','Responsive, accessibility and language QA',f'{ev("responsive-a11y-results.json")} records312 route/locale/theme geometry observations over widths320/360/390/430/600/768/820/1024/1440/1920 and844×390,820×430,768×390. No measured horizontal input clipping/overflow.49 axe runs comprise48 ordinary initial/error scenes and one forced-colors scan. The latter retains a computed custom-color contrast finding; the captured actual forced palette is readable black/white/blue on visual inspection. It is not silently turned into a zero-finding WCAG claim.\n\n{ev("contrast-results.json")} computes selected text/background samples with alpha blending. Placeholder/border/focus variants are not all certified by that sample set. C08 pending browser test checks real pointer/keyboard toggle focus and selection; live alerts and labels remain.\n\nPhysical iOS/Android, native keyboard occlusion/safe-area, hardware keyboard, native200/400% zoom/OS scaling, VoiceOver/TalkBack and native Khmer terminology remain unverified external/manual gates. Geometry emulation is not native zoom. Normal/reduced motion has legacy browser coverage; the full every-state cross-product is not claimed.')
doc('12-performance-network-payload-and-runtime.md','Performance and payload evidence',f'{ev("build-assets.json")} records every emitted final HTML/JS/CSS raw/gzip/Brotli separately for user/admin. These totals are not initial route transfer; public media is excluded. Gemini’s382kB main chunk claim is stale. No runtime dependency was added.\n\n{ev("performance-comparison.json")} aggregates three samples per route×cold/repeat-navigation condition,18 before and18 after. Native browser FCP/LCP/CLS clocks and resource transfer/duration arrays are retained in before/after-performance.json. Interception disables HTTP cache; repeat navigation is not a true warm-cache sample. Zero LCP means observation not yet reported, not instant paint. No baseline all-chunk Brotli inventory, CPU/3G acceptance, device benchmark, field p75 or INP is certified. Variance and fixture/provider errors limit causal speed claims.\n\nPerformance remains REVIEW REQUIRED; current large marketing background, font range and Studio catalog remain owned carryovers, not Phase08 optimization targets.')
doc('13-browser-fixtures-states-and-visual-evidence.md','Fixture and capture provenance',f'{source("apps/frontend-user/tests/e2e/support/phase06Fixtures.js")} wraps bounded Batch12 DTOs with fictional identities, local-only resource policy and locale/theme seeds. Unknown API reads501 and unspecified writes405; each auth mutation/error is explicitly intercepted. No backend call is silently given a happy200. {source("apps/frontend-user/tests/e2e/phase08-codex-regression.spec.js")} exercises actual form controls and response handling.\n\n{ev("browser-coverage.json")}, {ev("visual-capture-manifest.json")} and per-command artifacts name exact origins, viewports, engine projects, data scope, hashes and logs.24 initial scenes are paired with repaired scenes; later error scenes are after-only. Actual scroll positions explain sticky headers appearing partway through full-page captures.\n\nPNG, trace and command logs under output/phase08-codex-2026-11-18 are **LOCAL — NOT COMMITTED**. Regenerate current captures with `node docs/uxui/phase08-codex-identity-account-audit-2026-11-18/evidence/capture.mjs after after-reproduced`; run tests through audit.py to archive artifacts. Do not regenerate before evidence from repaired code. All identities/tokens are fictional; clear sensitive input controls before captured API-error states.')
doc('14-confirmed-defects-fixes-and-reproduction.md','Confirmed defects and repairs',f'{ev("defect-register.json")} holds12 stable IDs, affected source, reproduction, before/after tests, security impact and rollback scope. No P0/P1 was proven; eleven P2 and one P3. Initial independent new unit run reproduced14 failures/2 passes across seven groups, provider retry and registration DTO edge have separate failing runs, aliases failed in both browser projects and contrast has raw before findings.\n\n'+table(['ID','Severity','Finding','Repair and regression'],[(r['id'],r['severity'],r['title'],r['fix']+' '+r['tests'])for r in defects])+f'\n\n{ev("gemini-defect-validation.json")} independently resolves all six DEF-08 IDs; several were pre-existing behavior or overstated claims, not six newly reproduced Gemini fixes.')
doc('15-exact-test-commands-results-and-known-failure-register.md','Exact commands, failures and limitations',f'{ev("test-command-results.json")} is the complete recorded run ledger with source fingerprints, timestamps, environment overrides and local logs. Parallel runner entries also have individual runs/*.json files. Commands below actually executed; later passes never erase earlier failures.\n\n'+table(['ID','Exact child command','Environment','Actual result'],[(r['id'],'`'+r['command']+'`',r.get('environment',{}),result(r['id']))for r in records])+"\n\nFailure classification: negative-first and negative-provider are intentional pre-repair contracts; repaired-auth failures identified obsolete Gemini privacy/delivery expectations plus a multi-status selector; final-user-unit had a new happy-dom script-node timing assumption, corrected using captured appended nodes; codex-browser-initial had ambiguous alert locators plus the real alias loss; user-lint flagged the missing node:buffer import. First final capture used an English-only token label in Khmer, corrected by a locale-independent control selector without changing product behavior. Initial Phase04–06 had exactly two preview URL-origin mismatches. Phase02 retains original six known red assertions; no assertion or copy was weakened.\n\nAdditional attempted tooling: Maven was absent from PATH; initial wrapper invocation had a PowerShell comma parse error and relative executable resolution error. Absolute repository mvnw.cmd succeeded29 tests. Python Brotli import was unavailable; Node built-in zlib generated the exact inventory instead. No package was installed to bypass these limits. Read-only guessed-path/PowerShell-brace searches were corrected. Full backend/payment suites, live DB/provider tests and physical/native/field tests were not run. Unit harness logs include expected disabled external-resource warnings/localhost connection refusals; exit/count evidence distinguishes these from failing assertions.")
