doc('17-cross-phase-57-item-plus-new-gates.md','57 historical items and separate new gates',f'Historical status distribution is unchanged: `{carry["counts"]}`. Every57 original ID/owner/status retained; zero speculative closures. Five AUTH IDs are new additions, making62 rows if combined, not57 with34 verified. Gemini’s category arithmetic mixed these denominators.\n\n'+table(['Original ID','Inherited status','Owner','Next action'],[(r['id'],r['finalStatus'],r['owner'],r.get('nextAction')or r.get('requiredFix'))for r in carry['entries']])+table(['Separate AUTH item','Independent status','Evidence'],[(r['id'],r['status'],r['evidence'])for r in carry['newPhase08Items']])+f'\n\nPhase07 retains9 partial marketing gates in {ev("phase07-partial-gates.json")}; venues/media rights/facts,2.40MiB background, SEO crawler fallback, device/native copy and field/runner review are not closed by auth tests. See next owners in the unchanged ledger and Phase09.1 handoff.')
doc('18-files-changed-risk-security-and-safe-rollback.md','Changed files and selective rollback',f'{ev("changed-files-attribution.json")} lists only Codex source/test overlays with baseline/final hashes and unified hunk ranges. {ev("codex-only.patch")} is generated against immutable starting bytes or clean HEAD for originally untouched source, not against the entire dirty tree. `git apply --reverse --check docs/uxui/phase08-codex-identity-account-audit-2026-11-18/evidence/codex-only.patch` is a dry run only. Actual reversal requires review and a fresh byte check; no reversal was performed. Do not use checkout/restore/reset/clean or Gemini rm recipes. New reports are independent files; remove only explicitly reviewed Codex-created files if later authorized.\n\nProtected-source hash validation includes backend/Telegram/admin, migrations/SQL, manifests/lockfiles, templates/registry/art/font assets. No protected source changed. User auth store and host account pill/alias are explicitly in scope: session invalidation, responsive CSS and account return repair, with full frontend and representative shell/browser checks. The index.html overlay only adds early no-referrer, preserving all Phase07 preload/metadata work. Prior reports remain byte-identical. Existing editor unknown JSON, preview origin/nonce trust, RSVP/guest privacy, media ownership, settlement/entitlements, USD/KHR and licensing are not modified. No real credentials/accounts, production writes, staged files, commit, push or deployment.')
doc('19-phase09-1-gemini-frontend-execution-handoff.md','Phase09.1 Gemini execution handoff',f'**Next owner: Gemini frontend implementation. Subsequent Phase09 owner: Codex independent QA/repair. Phase09 has not been implemented here.**\n\nStart at the actual dirty main `{baseline["head"]}`,13 commits ahead of the observed origin. Read MASTER_SCOPE Phase09 and its global dependencies, ROUTER.md, this package and preserved Phase07/08 reports. Do not reset, stage, commit, push, deploy or apply the earlier destructive rollback recipe. Establish new before evidence from the actual local source; preserve the Codex-only auth patch, privacy and password policies, account/alias/host contrast repairs and marketing work.\n\nResolve current `/templates`, `/templates/browse`, `/templates/browse/:id`, `/templates/:slug`, `/templates/:slug/preview`, `/templates/:slug/checkout`, `/pricing` and `/app/packages` from current route inventory before changing them. Implement discovery/category/search/filter/sort, template detail/demo, responsive plans/comparisons and truthful purchase/return guidance using current DTOs. Treat `/templates/browse` as guarded and preserve validated template-to-create next intent. Protect server prices and paid/owned flags, USD/KHR separation, ABA PayWay/pending/verified statuses, ownership and entitlements. A public preview/demo never grants paid access. Registry IDs,38 static aliases,10 authored renderers, shared IDs/fallback and preview origin/nonce protocols remain independent. No fake discount/inventory, favorite service, live AI, booking API or payment success.\n\nRequired matrix: EN/KM, light/dark, responsive/short landscape, reduced motion, empty/loading/error/denied states, unavailable catalog/media fallback, keyboard filters/drawer/fullscreen preview and continuation after authentication. Preserve drafts/unknown JSON. Record before/after, API boundaries, exact functional/axe/contrast/performance evidence and isolated provider/DB/device limits.\n\nTransfer every row of57-carryover-updated.json, the five separate AUTH entries and nine Phase07 partials. Native Khmer/physical AT/zoom/live Google/Telegram/SMTP/storage/DB/field metrics remain external/manual; cookie browser breadth, every-state accessibility, provider localization and default-worker reliability need named follow-up. Phone-only recovery is a backend/product service gap, not a Telegram support feature. Preserve Phase02 QA-NEW-01/02/03 red assertions until copy/QA owner approves replacements. Prepare a precise handoff for Phase09 Codex, but do not generate or execute that independent prompt now.')
